From e361f58d9d974e1fb5ebfc0920b6d272240af00f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Onni Hakala <onni@flaky.build>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:44:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Reuse type check results of dependents with warnings

The type check result of each module is stored in the manifest as its grouped
type diagnostics. When a runtime dependent is verified again because a module
it calls was recompiled with the same ExCk chunk, its previous result is
reported again instead of type checking it, so its warnings are printed
exactly as before. Behaviour checks and @after_verify callbacks still run.

Phoenix app with a type warning in the router: editing a LiveView no longer
type checks the router, mix compile 0.45s -> 0.39s.
